Subject: [PATCH v9 0/2] arm64: dts: qcom: describe the USB-C receptacles of the Lenovo Y700 Gen4

*** AI-assistance disclosure ***
This series was prepared with the help of an LLM coding assistant.  The
author reviewed every line, checked every quoted claim against the tree and
ran the gates quoted below; the design decisions and any errors are the
author's.

The Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen 4 (SM8750) has two USB Type-C receptacles that
share the controller's High Speed D+/D- pair through an analog 2:1 mux
whose select input is TLMM GPIO 29.  This series labels the DWC3 High Speed
port node in sm8750.dtsi, then describes the mux, the select line and one
usb-c-connector per receptacle in the board file, with one endpoint per
receptacle on port@0 so the role switch code can follow remote-endpoint to
the connector that is actually in use.

Dependency: this series needs the DWC3 two-connector binding ("usb: dwc3:
support two connectors sharing one HS data bus", posted separately).  The
binding adds "mux-controls", "mux-state" and "usb-role-switch" on the
endpoints of port@0; without it the board file is reported with
"mux-controls", "mux-state" and "usb-role-switch" as unexpected properties.
The board series of 2026-11-17 ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750-lenovo-elden: add
Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen 4", v7) deliberately did not describe USB at all;
this series adds that part now that the binding exists.

Known gaps (stated so that nobody has to guess)

- Which receptacle corresponds to mux state 0 and which to 1 is not proven
  on hardware: no schematic sheet names GPIO 29 and the two vendor sources
  disagree about its polarity.  The two states only say that the endpoints
  differ, which is what the binding requires.
- The mux node carries no "idle-state": the role mux deselects the old port
  right before selecting the new one, and an explicit idle state would be
  driven in between, glitching both receptacles.
- Which USB role belongs to which connector at boot is left to the role
  switch of each connector; no runtime testing of the mux path is claimed
  for this version.

